############################################################################
#
#       Name:   bench_icnrel_isolate.icn
#
#       Title:  RTX-6b-ICN isolation benchmark -- rt_jct_relop string arm
#
############################################################################
#
#  Exercises the arm measured live at s212: DT_S/DT_S operands under the
#  string relational operators, which fall past every numeric arm of
#  rt_jct_relop_impl to its textually LAST block (VARVAL_fn + strcmp).
#
#  TWO PROPERTIES THIS PROGRAM IS BUILT AROUND, BOTH LEARNED THE HARD WAY:
#
#  1. PRISTINE KERNEL (CEO-567, CEO-1221; hq_icon 2026-09-23).  Until 2026-09-23 this program timed
#     itself with &time and wrote "ms: " for the harness.  The timing now belongs to the generated
#     wrapper (fixed iterations, fixed time, process wrapper), which also excludes the compile phase
#     -- the reason the window used to live in the source.  The source computes and prints its
#     result signature, which its .ref pins; nothing else.
#
#  2. ALLOCATION IS HOISTED OUT OF THE TIMED LOOP (s211).  The first
#     RTX-6 benchmark was REFUSED by the harness because per-iteration
#     allocation made its samples bimodal, with an intra-arm spread larger
#     than the gap being measured.  Every string here is built once, before
#     the window opens; the loop allocates nothing.
#
#  Integer comparison is deliberately ABSENT.  bb_binop_relop.cpp inlines
#  DT_I/DT_I and reaches gamma without a call, so an integer comparison
#  measures the template, not this symbol.  The loop counter's own `1 to n`
#  is the only integer work and it is identical across all three arms.
#
#  N is edited into the source: mode 3 does not forward argv
#  (`scrip --run p.icn -n8` => cannot open '-n8'), which is the open half
#  of RTX-0b-ICN.
#
############################################################################

procedure main()
   local i, n, c, eqa, eqb, ne, lo, hi;

   n := 5000000;
   c := 0;

   eqa := "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog";
   eqb := "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog";
   ne  := "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dof";
   lo  := "aardvark astonishes the arbitrary alphabet";
   hi  := "zeppelin zigzags through zealous zookeepers";

   every i := 1 to n do {
      if eqa == eqb then c := c + 1;
      if eqa == ne  then c := c + 2;
      if lo  << hi  then c := c + 4;
      if hi  >> lo  then c := c + 8;
      if eqa ~== ne then c := c + 16;
      if lo  <<= hi then c := c + 32
   };

   write("chk: ", c);

end
